Goom2k26 — copyright and licensing notice
=========================================

Goom2k26 is a revival of Goom, the music visualizer effect engine
originally developed by Jean-Christophe Hoelt and Guillaume Borios,
with contributions from Florent Boudet, released 2000-2003 under the
informal group name "iOS-software" (a hobbyist developer group, no
relation to Apple Inc. or its iOS operating system).

The Goom core sources carry the "LGPL Licence" notice from the
original releases. This distribution licenses the whole Goom2k26
tree under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1
(see the LICENSE file in this directory).

Copyright holders:
  - Goom core (Goom/):            (c)2000-2003 Jean-Christophe Hoelt;
                                  Guillaume Borios (PPC/AltiVec zoom filter,
                                  CPU detection)
                                  (c)2026 the Goom2k26 contributors
  - Engine layers (gametools/, iosfc/, sdl/, libs/ additions):
                                  (c)2003-2012 Jean-Christophe Hoelt (Fovea.cc),
                                  with Guillaume Borios and Florent Boudet
                                  (c)2026 the Goom2k26 contributors

If you use this library in a visual program, credit is appreciated:
a visible mention of Goom and its original authors in your about
screen or documentation is the historical convention of this codebase.

Vendored third-party components keep their own licenses:
  - libs/soil         — public domain / MIT (includes GLFreeType, FTL via freetype)
  - freetype2 (linked, not vendored) — FTL or GPL-2.0, at your option

Note for Android/other closed-source distributions: the Goom core
is also available under this LGPL license; application-layer glue
and platform bindings are separate works.